## Solution

### Fix 1 — VMSS CPU alerts (≈ 20 min)
Add `Percentage CPU` metric alert per VMSS, route to existing action group.

```bash
SUB=a9049f9f-3d1b-43f0-9278-7f1d603f6a00
AG_PROD=$(az monitor action-group show -g rg-normain-prod-01 -n ag-alerts-normain-prod-01 --query id -o tsv --subscription $SUB)

# Prod VMSS
PROD_VMSS=$(az vmss show -g MC_rg-normain-prod-01_aks-normain-prod-01_swedencentral -n aks-default-31982391-vmss --query id -o tsv --subscription $SUB)
az monitor metrics alert create -n vmss-cpu-alert-normain-prod-01 \
  -g rg-normain-prod-01 --subscription $SUB --scopes $PROD_VMSS \
  --condition "avg Percentage CPU > 80" \
  --window-size 15m --evaluation-frequency 5m --severity 2 --action $AG_PROD

# Dev VMSS — only if dev is in audit scope
DEV_VMSS=$(az vmss show -g MC_rg-normain-dev-20_aks-normain-dev-20_swedencentral -n aks-default-25586624-vmss --query id -o tsv --subscription $SUB)
az monitor metrics alert create -n vmss-cpu-alert-normain-dev-20 \
  -g rg-normain-dev-20 --subscription $SUB --scopes $DEV_VMSS \
  --condition "avg Percentage CPU > 80" \
  --window-size 15m --evaluation-frequency 5m --severity 2 --action $AG_PROD
```
Alert scoped at the VMSS resource covers all instances (`_0`, `_2`, `_51`, future).

### Fix 2 — Storage account availability alerts (≈ 30 min)

```bash
SUB=a9049f9f-3d1b-43f0-9278-7f1d603f6a00
AG_PROD=$(az monitor action-group show -g rg-normain-prod-01 -n ag-alerts-normain-prod-01 --query id -o tsv --subscription $SUB)

declare -A ACCOUNTS=(
  [rpsnormainprod01]=rg-normain-prod-01
  [dssnormainprod01]=rg-normain-prod-01
  [auinormainprod01]=rg-normain-prod-01
  [normaintfappproduction]=normain-tf-app-production
  [normainfglobal]=normain-tf-global
  [normaintfidentity]=normain-tf-identity
  [rpsnormaindev20]=rg-normain-dev-20
  [dssnormaindev20]=rg-normain-dev-20
  [auinormaindev20]=rg-normain-dev-20
  [normaintfappdevelopment]=normain-tf-app-development
)
for acc in "${!ACCOUNTS[@]}"; do
  rg=${ACCOUNTS[$acc]}
  id=$(az storage account show -n $acc -g $rg --query id -o tsv --subscription $SUB)
  az monitor metrics alert create -n "storage-availability-alert-${acc}" \
    -g $rg --subscription $SUB --scopes $id \
    --condition "avg Availability < 99" \
    --window-size 15m --evaluation-frequency 5m --severity 2 --action $AG_PROD
done
```

